# Rank 1735 / CVE-2024-46898: SHIRASAGI's public page controller resolves the
# request path to a file under the site's public directory and sends it, with no
# canonicalisation between the two (CWE-22). ApplicationController#request_path
# is the raw value:
#
#   def request_path
#     request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
#   end
#
# and Cms::PublicFilter, mixed into Cms::PublicController, threads it through
# three before_action methods into the send:
#
#   def set_request_path
#     @cur_path ||= request_path
#     ...
#   end
#   def parse_path
#     @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
#     @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
#   end
#   def x_sendfile(file = @file)
#     return unless Fs.file?(file)
#     ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
#   end
#
# File.join keeps the `..` components, so a request path of
# `docs/../../../../<rails-root>/README.md` escapes the site directory and the
# file is served inline. The fixed revision 5ac4685d7e4330f949f13219069107fc5d768934 adds
# SS.request_path(request), which runs the path through
# `Addressable::URI.parse(...).normalize.request_uri` — normalisation resolves
# the dot segments, so the joined path stays under the site root — and routes
# every request.path use through it. The fix touches only
# application_controller.rb's request_path body and app/models/ss.rb;
# concerns/cms/public_filter.rb is identical across the pair, so only the taint
# path through request_path discriminates, and a binding keyed on the filter's
# own shape cannot tell the revisions apart.
#
# Both ends are labelled: `request.env` is code.HttpInput (binding
# httpInput12, m5a48bf47.vyql:72) and `send_file` is code.FilePathAccess
# (binding filePathAccess143, m5a48bf47.vyql:779, firing at
# application_controller.rb:100), so VYQL-PATH-001 needs only a taint path
# between them. Three Ruby frontend gaps sit on that path, and the first test
# below pins the resulting miss. None of them is a binding problem.
#
# 1. A receiverless, paren-less call names no callee the resolver can match.
#    `request_path` in Ruby is an `identifier` node, indistinguishable from a
#    local variable read without scope tracking, so no Call node exists and the
#    trace dead-ends at `analysis.function.return`. `self.request_path` does
#    produce a Call, but with path `?.request_path` — the `self` receiver is
#    dropped rather than substituted with the enclosing class, the same gap
#    PHP's `dotted()` fixed for `self::`/`static::`. `request_path()` (parens,
#    no receiver) resolves and carries taint, which is why the third test's
#    inlined form reports.
# 2. An instance variable written in one method is not read in another.
#    `@cur_main_path` is assigned in `set_request_path` and consumed in
#    `parse_path`; a two-method pair with nothing else on the path reports
#    nothing, while the same assignment and read inside one method reports.
#    Ruby has no field-sensitive interprocedural summary, and Rails controller
#    concerns are built almost entirely out of exactly this shape.
# 3. A defaulted parameter does not see its default. `def x_sendfile(file = @file)`
#    lowers the body with `file` unbound to `@file`; the method is only ever
#    invoked through `before_action :x_sendfile`, so no call site supplies the
#    argument either.
#
# A fourth gap on this path is fixed: `operator_assignment` in rbConv.stmt
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/ruby.go:393) accepts the same target
# kinds as the plain assignment case beside it, so `@cur_path ||= request_path()`
# carries taint — Ruby memoises with `@x ||= expr` everywhere — and the fourth
# test pins that live half. Fixing it alone does not make the real shape
# detectable, and gaps 1 to 3 are not mechanical: 1 needs scope tracking to
# tell a call from a variable read, 2 is a new interprocedural dataflow
# relation, 3 needs default substitution wired into parameter lowering.
# Fixing any one of them alone leaves the path broken — with the parens form
# the trace advances into `@cur_path.dup` and stops again.
#
# Re-measured on the real checkout at 5ac4685d^ and 5ac4685d over three
# --cache off runs per revision (`timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off
# --max-ram 6GB` over app/controllers, 1184 Ruby files): the full findings
# view reports 459 findings every run at both revisions, 27 of them
# VYQL-PATH-001, and none has a source in concerns/cms/public_filter.rb or in
# ApplicationController#request_path — the six findings added since the first
# measurement (453) come from Ruby bindings shipped afterwards, none on this
# shape. Both ends still label (`request.env` code.HttpInput at
# application_controller.rb:137, `send_file` code.FilePathAccess at :100), and
# `vyql trace -from code.HttpInput -to code.FilePathAccess` still dead-ends at
# `analysis.function.return` on the bare `request_path` call while the parens
# form advances.
#
# When scope tracking, an instance-variable summary and parameter defaults land
# for Ruby, the first test must flip to expect and the second stays reject.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1735: the request path joined onto the site directory and served inline"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/application_controller.rb
  code
  ```
  class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
    private

    def request_path
      request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
    end

    def ss_send_file(file_or_path, opts = {})
      send_file file_or_path, opts
    end
  end
  ```
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      before_action :set_request_path
      before_action :parse_path
      before_action :x_sendfile
    end

    def set_request_path
      @cur_path ||= request_path
      @cur_main_path = @cur_path.dup
    end

    def parse_path
      @cur_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
    end

    def x_sendfile(file = @file)
      return unless Fs.file?(file)
      ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: the path is normalised before it is joined onto the site directory"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/application_controller.rb
  code
  ```
  module SS
    def request_path(request)
      Addressable::URI.parse(request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path).normalize.request_uri
    end
  end

  class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
    include SS

    private

    def request_path
      @request_path ||= SS.request_path(request)
    end

    def ss_send_file(file_or_path, opts = {})
      send_file file_or_path, opts
    end
  end
  ```
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    extend ActiveSupport::Concern

    included do
      before_action :set_request_path
      before_action :parse_path
      before_action :x_sendfile
    end

    def set_request_path
      @cur_path ||= request_path
      @cur_main_path = @cur_path.dup
    end

    def parse_path
      @cur_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @cur_main_path.sub!(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      @file = File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_main_path)
    end

    def x_sendfile(file = @file)
      return unless Fs.file?(file)
      ss_send_file(file, type: Fs.content_type(file), disposition: :inline)
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: the same join and send report once the request path is read inline"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/concerns/cms/public_filter.rb
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  module Cms::PublicFilter
    def index
      cur_path = request.env["REQUEST_PATH"] || request.path
      cur_main_path = cur_path.sub(/\/$/, "/index.html")
      file = File.join(@cur_site.path, cur_main_path)
      send_file file, type: "text/html", disposition: :inline
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1735: a memoised request path keeps its taint through the op-assign"
  lang ruby
  file app/controllers/cms/public_controller.rb
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  class Cms::PublicController < ApplicationController
    def index
      @cur_path ||= params[:path]
      send_file File.join(@cur_site.path, @cur_path), disposition: :inline
    end
  end
  ```
